# Rollout-Aware KV-Cache Efficiency for High-Resolution VLM Reinforcement Learning

> **Project brief for the research engineer / coding agent**  
> **Primary goal:** reduce redundant visual-prompt computation during repeated VLM rollouts by improving reuse, retention, and scheduling of cache state under tight GPU-memory budgets.  
> **Initial scope:** systems-only. Do not change the model architecture, train a new router/RPN, or change the RL objective until the existing execution path has been profiled and a cache optimization has been demonstrated.

This README is intended to be the complete handoff. The agent working from the repository may not have access to the original 60-slide project deck or prior discussion. The relevant project context, measurements, open questions, links, and proposed workflow are captured below.

