## 12. Suggested implementation milestones

### Milestone 0 — Environment / code-path report

Deliver a short note listing actual runtime versions, paths traced, cache settings and where the cache is allocated, reused, and evicted. No patch required.

### Milestone 1 — Reproducible cache benchmark

Deliver a minimal script or test harness reproducing same-prefix rollout requests, prewarm/no-prewarm, wave-size and encoder-cache budget sweeps. Save structured logs and a summary table. Establish whether the slide's observations reproduce in the current stack.

### Milestone 2 — Instrumented cache lifecycle

Add the smallest necessary metrics for decoder-prefix hits/misses/evictions/recomputed tokens and encoder-cache hits/misses/evictions/recomputed encoder work. Keep instrumentation configurable and low overhead. Submit a code-path diagram and sample trace.

### Milestone 3 — Baseline tuning / existing alternatives

Try configuration and scheduling changes first. Compare native prefix cache, encoder cache, CPU offloading, and LMCache where compatible. Identify the best non-new-method baseline.

### Milestone 4 — Candidate method

Based on evidence, propose 2–3 possible methods and rank them by expected speedup, risk, implementation cost, correctness risk and novelty. Then implement the most defensible minimal version behind a feature flag/config. Add unit/integration tests.

Potential candidates include rollout-group-aware scheduling, retention of high-reuse image/question prefix blocks, selective offload of expensive shared prefixes, or an alternative cache policy. These are options to evaluate, not decisions already made.

### Milestone 5 — Controlled evaluation

Run repeated paired tests against the best baseline under a fixed GPU-memory budget. Report speed/throughput, memory use, encoder and KV cache behavior, transfer overhead, output correctness, and accuracy/reward where relevant.

### Milestone 6 — End-to-end RL validation

After the systems-only win is established, run a small GRPO setup with a fixed number of questions and rollouts. Verify end-to-end step-time improvements across multiple policy updates and verify cache invalidation at each weight-version boundary. Only then scale the evaluation.

### Required deliverables

- `README.md` updates or a research note describing the actual implementation path;
- benchmark script(s) and exact run commands;
- raw logs plus an aggregation script/table;
- code change with tests and a feature flag/config if applicable;
- before/after comparison against the best existing baseline;
- a concise methodology note documenting what is novel, what prior art already does, and remaining limitations.

